 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "roads lists [from, to, duration] triples; every location has at most one outgoing road, \"Campground\" has none, and every route ends at \"Campground\". friends lists [name, home] pairs with distinct names. Driver 1 starts at start1 and driver 2 at start2 (different locations, neither the Campground) at time 0. A driver reaches a location after the sum of the durations along its route. Every friend's home lies on at least one route (never the Campground). A friend whose home is on one route rides with that driver; when the home is on both routes, the friend rides with the driver who reaches it first (driver 1 on a tie). Return [driver 1 passengers, driver 2 passengers], each in pickup order (friends at the same home in input order).",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk15-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
